WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:21.470
Okay.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:43.380
So pretty big news.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:48.380
In the last 24 hours, the governor of New
York, Andrew Cuomo, has signed a bill, which

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:54.440
would allow the release of Donald Trump's
state tax returns from the state of New York

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.420
specifically to one or up to three different
congressional committees.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:02.110
Now, there are some people who think this
is the biggest deal in the world.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:05.359
There are, Trump is too are saying this is
nothing.

00:01:05.359 --> 00:01:09.100
And the truth is that it's potentially a moderately
big deal.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.659
Remember, this is not Donald Trump's federal
taxes.

00:01:11.659 --> 00:01:13.909
This is his New York state taxes.

00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:18.880
Andrew Cuomo signed a bill yesterday, which
would allow three congressional committees

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:26.920
access to Trump state tax returns from New
York for a quote specified and legitimate

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.929
legislative purpose.

00:01:27.929 --> 00:01:32.849
So now the three committees, if they want
to request Trump's New York state tax returns

00:01:32.849 --> 00:01:37.740
on this basis, they're going to have to demonstrate
what is the specific legitimate legislative

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.599
purpose for obtaining Donald Trump's tax returns.

00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:45.229
The three committees are the house ways and
means committee, the Senate Finance Committee,

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:48.969
and the joint committee on taxation, which
includes members of both the House and Senate.

00:01:48.969 --> 00:01:52.140
So number one, there's still a very long way
to go here.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:56.399
Can they actually demonstrate a specific and
legitimate legislative purpose?

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:02.319
Number two, can Donald Trump or any other
agency or department challenged this in total,

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:07.610
like challenge the law in total or specifically
challenge or request on the basis of that

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:13.530
particular request, not being a have but not
demonstrating a specific and legitimate legislative

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:14.560
purpose.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:20.500
Number three, would the New York state tax
return if we were to see it, give us all or

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.300
most of the same information as Trump's federal
tax return?

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.940
The answer to that is we wouldn't get everything
from a New York state return that we would

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.930
from a federal tax return, but we would get
most of it.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:35.670
And I am interested in this and I want to
see Donald Trump's taxes, but this is one

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.980
of those things where it's really important
for the left to manage expectations.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:43.250
Should Donald Trump have released his tax
returns from the beginning?

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.250
Absolutely.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.470
Do we want to see Donald Trump's tax returns
at this point in time?

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.810
Uh, even this late in the game?

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:50.810
Absolutely.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:51.810
We do.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:57.920
Our Trump's tax returns likely to reveal anything
that would be a blockbuster in terms of either

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.010
exposing criminality or effecting Donald Trump's
reelection.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.010
It's not likely.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.010
It's, it's just not likely.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:08.260
It could expose that Donald Trump is not as
rich as he says, but his followers don't care.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.530
They'll find excuses.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:14.600
It might expose that Donald Trump pays very
little in taxes, but his followers will say

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.600
that makes him smart.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.890
Well, that's the benefit of being in the Republican
Party that wants taxes lower, lower, lower,

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:23.591
no matter what the consequences that if you
find a way not to pay taxes as Donald Trump

00:03:23.591 --> 00:03:28.740
may have successfully done for a long time
or pay very little in taxes, that's not, that's

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.990
seen as a feature, not a bug by the people
you're to get to vote for you.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:37.370
And then lastly, uh, Richard Neil, my old
congressman from Massachusetts, who's the

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:44.290
person, uh, who has to request the tax returns
so far has said he's not going to request

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:49.160
them under this new law that he's going to,
I guess keep working on getting the federal

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.600
tax returns through some other means or something
like that.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:58.630
Um, so this is news and I want to see the
tax returns, but it's important not to get

00:03:58.630 --> 00:03:59.720
carried away here.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.130
Let's keep an eye on what matters.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.250
We want to stop Republican bills from becoming
the law.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.470
We want to get Donald Trump out in 2020.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.739
We want to pick up seats in the house in 2020.

00:04:08.739 --> 00:04:13.240
We want to, to difficult map in the Senate
for Democrats in 2020, but we want to try

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:20.949
to not lose seats in the Senate as the case
may be and set up the 2022 election to maybe

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:23.879
lead to taking over control of the Senate.

00:04:23.879 --> 00:04:27.810
And we need to, by the way, I keep saying
this and I've been saying it for years.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:34.010
We need to make sure that the census is done
and done correctly while we continue fighting

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:40.520
voter suppression so that everybody who wants
to vote in 2020 not only is allowed to vote

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:46.310
but has their vote counted, which is another
layer that a, um, uh, Republicans have been

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:51.759
working very, very hard to destroy as a function
of democracy for many years, if not more than

00:04:51.759 --> 00:04:53.190
a decade at this point in time.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.689
So let's hopefully see the tax returns.

00:04:55.689 --> 00:04:57.639
The tax returns are not going to be the blockbuster.

00:04:57.639 --> 00:05:01.379
That may be some belief and much like, you
know, we would, if you were waiting around

00:05:01.379 --> 00:05:05.810
for the molar report to say, we have video
of Trump and Putin personally colluding, you

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.400
are waiting for something all along.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.499
That was never going to happen.

00:05:08.499 --> 00:05:12.819
In the same way, if you're waiting for Trump's
tax returns to be such a blockbuster bombshell

00:05:12.819 --> 00:05:17.099
that they lead to his removal or impeachment,
I mean it's just not going to happen.

00:05:17.099 --> 00:05:18.049
And I would focus on things we can control.

